WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.024 --> 00:00:04.745
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.745 --> 00:00:06.680
What's your ambition?

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.950
Take a second, pause and think about it.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.808
What's an ambition that you have for
yourself?

00:00:14.808 --> 00:00:18.380
Whether it's to become
the next Blockchain investor.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.760
To launch that start up
you've always dreamed of, or

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.910
to become the next secretary of defense.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.690
Whatever it might be,

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:31.360
imagine how amazing you're going to
feel when you realize that ambition.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.070
Now, let's just say I arbitrarily
decide to draw a line down the room,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.960
include Jodie in the line on this side.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.650
I tell all of you on this
side of the room, but

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.140
actually, just because I decided,
you don't get to realize your ambition,

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.830
because you sat in that seat, you don't
get the opportunity to pursue your dreams.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:01:00.436
Imagine how much it would suck to have
your ambition taken away from you.

00:01:00.436 --> 00:01:04.566
This is what happens to
women all over the world.

00:01:04.566 --> 00:01:09.220
Let me walk you across the world for
a second, to a rural part of Kenya.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:15.420
It's a scorching hot day, and
I'm sitting under a shady tree, talking to

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.400
a bunch of girls and asking them that same
question that I just asked all of you.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.120
What's your ambition?

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:30.100
The girls respond, to be a doctor,
to be a lawyer, to be an astronaut.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:35.160
Just like you and me, these girls
imagine a bright future for themselves.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.850
Yet as my conversation
with them continues,

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.190
I begin to realize that they're not
going to realize their ambition.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.180
That because of factors
beyond their control,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.330
they won't have the opportunity
to pursue their dreams.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.458
One of the girls, Dorothy,
who I got to know well during this time,

00:01:56.458 --> 00:02:00.840
tells me that every morning,
she wakes up at 4 AM before school.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:07.590
And she walks two hours to a well gets
water and carries it home for her family.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:13.350
After school, she's the one who's expected
to take care of her younger siblings, and

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.450
cook dinner for the family.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.521
While Dorothy's brothers are studying,
her and

00:02:20.521 --> 00:02:26.878
millions of girls like around the world,
are expected to on household work.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:34.027
When money is tied parents sent a clear
signal by sending their sons to school but

00:02:34.027 --> 00:02:36.710
asking their daughters to stay home.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.597
And when girls do make
it to the classroom,

00:02:40.597 --> 00:02:45.484
they have to listen to their teachers make
comments like, don't do math like a girl.

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:51.623
Girls are constantly told implicitly and
explicitly,

00:02:51.623 --> 00:02:56.710
that their ambitions are not as
important as their brothers.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.380
And what does this mean?

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.970
This means that less than
15% of the girls that

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.860
I met that summer will
graduate from high school.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:15.890
Their ambitions of being doctors,
lawyers, and astronauts will get crushed.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:23.150
And instead they'll get married young,
give birth to multiple children, and

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:29.364
then they'll ask their daughters to stay
at home and help with household tasks.

00:03:29.364 --> 00:03:33.531
Their daughters will become
the next generation of women

00:03:33.531 --> 00:03:35.626
who have to carry the water.

00:03:38.261 --> 00:03:41.397
This is the heartbreaking reality of so

00:03:41.397 --> 00:03:46.533
many of the girls who I met in Muhuru Bay,
Kenya seven years ago.

00:03:48.006 --> 00:03:53.877
At that time, I was thinking what some
of you might be thinking right now.

00:03:53.877 --> 00:03:59.175
This is extremely sad, but
it's also kind of expected

00:03:59.175 --> 00:04:03.789
in a low income and
rural place like Muhuru Bay.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.070
I left the situation
feeling totally helpless,

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:13.960
I wanted to make a difference but
didn't know how.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:18.410
Several years later I decided to apply to
Stanford's Graduate school of Business.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.900
When I got the infamous call
from Derek Bolton, I was elated

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.340
I was so excited, and
I thought that such a well-resourced and

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.950
elite place like the JSB, I would
find my answers to these questions.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.760
I also assumed that for the first time
in my life, I would be in an environment

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.570
where women's ambition was not
only encouraged it was expected.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:53.007
However, I haven't always
found that to be the case.

00:04:53.007 --> 00:04:56.970
Let me take you to an override a couple of
months ago with a couple of classmates.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:02.290
Maybe some of you in the room we're riding
back home after a late night of BPL so

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.580
another night at the patio.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.300
There's a female classmate and
two close guy friends who are in a car.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.110
And we started joking around
about being single at the GSB,

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:13.959
some of you will also be
able to relate to that.

00:05:13.959 --> 00:05:17.520
[LAUGH] We were talking about
how rough it can be, and

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.729
those questions that constantly plague us.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.241
Should I bring a notebook on my
ambiguity date at abako tomorrow?

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:26.181
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:05:26.181 --> 00:05:27.921
&gt;&gt; Can one of you please create an Excel

00:05:27.921 --> 00:05:31.410
tracker so I can know who's still single?
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.530
&gt;&gt; But then all of a sudden

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.430
the conversation turned to
something I didn't expect.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:37.800
My female classmate turned to me and

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.110
said, Sadhna I don't think I'm going to
keep working once I get married.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:47.769
I doubt I'll find a husband who will
support my career ambition, I was shocked.

00:05:47.769 --> 00:05:50.380
This is Stanford's graduate
school of business.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.381
She went on to explain that
because women are more nurturing,

00:05:55.381 --> 00:05:59.620
it only makes sense that she is the only
expected to take care of her kids.

00:06:01.747 --> 00:06:06.100
And it turns out that my friend's
experience is not an anomaly.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.060
A recent Harvard business
review study shows,

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.660
that single MBA women continue
to downplay their ambition.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:20.517
They continue to feel like there is
a trade off between ambition and marriage.

00:06:20.517 --> 00:06:24.597
On the first day of the MBA program these
students were asked to state their career

00:06:24.597 --> 00:06:25.386
preferences.

00:06:25.386 --> 00:06:28.983
When they were told that their
responses would be shared with

00:06:28.983 --> 00:06:33.878
their male classmates, they said that
they wanted to make $20,000 less.

00:06:33.878 --> 00:06:38.508
They also said that they're less able and
willing to lead.

00:06:40.855 --> 00:06:43.670
Shouldn't this concern
everybody in the room?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:52.910
We want women to be smart, loving,
nurturing, but never ambitious.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:58.260
To be honest with you, I even hesitated
to give a talk on female ambition.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.679
Because I thought one of you
in the room would hear it, and

00:07:01.679 --> 00:07:03.613
think that I was too ambitious.

00:07:03.613 --> 00:07:06.614
And then I realized, this is the problem.

00:07:08.648 --> 00:07:13.258
Research also shows that
women in the US spend 25

00:07:13.258 --> 00:07:16.560
hours per week on household tasks.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:21.322
Women that are working, and
their male counterparts in the same

00:07:21.322 --> 00:07:26.448
professional tier spend only ten
hours per week on household tasks.

00:07:26.448 --> 00:07:30.657
So what shows up in the homes and
classrooms in Kenya,

00:07:30.657 --> 00:07:33.847
actually shows up right here at the GSB.

00:07:33.847 --> 00:07:39.213
Even in the United States,
women carry the water.

00:07:41.888 --> 00:07:46.353
No matter where we are,
and no matter how rich,

00:07:46.353 --> 00:07:49.712
how poor, there is a common theme.

00:07:49.712 --> 00:07:57.282
All across the development curve,
we fail to support women's ambition.

00:07:57.282 --> 00:08:01.290
It's easy to hear this talk and to not
realize the personal implications of it.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:07.723
To be honest, I didn't realize
it until it happened to me.

00:08:07.723 --> 00:08:12.409
I recently found myself in
a situation where I was told,

00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:15.712
that there was no room for my ambition.

00:08:15.712 --> 00:08:21.095
I was a three year relationship with
a guy who I loved and wanted to marry.

00:08:21.095 --> 00:08:25.411
Yet time and time again in
the relationship, there were so

00:08:25.411 --> 00:08:30.714
many subtle and some not so subtle
signs that my ambition was a problem.

00:08:32.013 --> 00:08:33.655
My partner's fear,

00:08:33.655 --> 00:08:38.953
that because I wanted to have a career
I wouldn't make a good mother.

00:08:38.953 --> 00:08:43.527
Or thoughts in my own head, that if I
just turn down my consulting offer after

00:08:43.527 --> 00:08:46.828
business school,
maybe I could make him love me more.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.855
But then in that moment,
I suddenly thought back to Dorothy, and

00:08:52.855 --> 00:08:55.009
all of the girls who I'd met in Kenya.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:01.430
I thought of my nine-year-old niece who
loves Bill Nye the Science Gu,y and

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.150
wants to be a scientist when she grows up.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.610
With their faces in my mind,
I finally gathered the courage

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:13.930
to leave the relationship rather
than to leave my ambition behind.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.590
In writing this talk I finally have
realized the answer to my question.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.490
I finally know what we can do
to help those girls in Kenya.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.635
And it starts with making
a change right here at the GSB.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:33.727
If you're a woman,
don't let someone else's expectations,

00:09:33.727 --> 00:09:36.031
dictate your level of ambition.

00:09:36.031 --> 00:09:39.992
Don't downplay your dreams for
somebody else.

00:09:39.992 --> 00:09:44.840
And if you're a man,
you play a huge role in all this.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:50.330
You have an amazing opportunity to
help women realize their ambition.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:54.452
Don't be afraid of ambitious women,
we don't bite, I promise.

00:09:54.452 --> 00:09:55.732
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:09:55.732 --> 00:09:58.150
&gt;&gt; Date ambitious women, marry them,

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:01.540
celebrate their accomplishments.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:07.691
In your future workplace, encourage women
to be ambitious and support their careers.

00:10:07.691 --> 00:10:11.162
And more tactically,
when you're in a domestic partnership,

00:10:11.162 --> 00:10:15.290
make sure you're taking on your share
of child's care and household work.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:22.380
Only then, when we all work together and
balance the load,

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:28.644
can we make sure that women aren't
the only ones carrying the water,

00:10:28.644 --> 00:10:33.791
thank you.
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:10:33.791 --> 00:10:36.793
[MUSIC]

